# Set the default behavior, in case people don't have core.autocrlf set.
* text=auto

# Check Go out with LF everywhere, including Windows.
#
# `text=auto` above stores LF but hands the working tree the platform's native
# ending, and gofmt's doc-comment normalization is sensitive to which it gets:
# given `/// x` it rewrites to `// / x` on LF input and leaves the line alone
# on CRLF. Same binary, same version -- only the line endings differ. That made
# the regen check pass on Linux and fail on Windows, where gofmt silently
# declined to reformat and the job reported a diff against a corpus every other
# platform produces.
*.go text eol=lf

# Rust and TypeScript too. scripts/generate_code.py hands the formatters LF and
# rewrites any CRLF file it formats, including ones nothing generated, which
# would make scripts/check_generate_code.py count them as regenerated.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
